that in the first place, care to elaborate on the subject you'd like to see discussed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-11T21:58:20-08:00","id":1530611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1530606-how-are-the-clan-and-the-covenant-opinion-on-psychic-vampire?p=1530610#post1530610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What you mean by that in the first place, care to elaborate on the subject you'd like to see discussed?</div> </div> </div> </div>I like to know, what does each of the Clan, The Covenant, and Vampire in general think of Psychic Vampire, the closest I've seen of a Psychic Vampire in Requiem is Amara, but that is only a single person rather than Psychic Vampire itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28270,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","user":"Yumlum","date":". 02-12-2024, 01:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T00:39:25-08:00","id":1530615,"title":"","content":"Do you not think of vampires with Auspex, including telepathy as psychic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T02:22:32-08:00","id":1530619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1530606-how-are-the-clan-and-the-covenant-opinion-on-psychic-vampire?p=1530615#post1530615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you not think of vampires with Auspex, including telepathy as psychic?</div> </div> </div> </div>When I mean &quot;Psychic Vampire&quot;, I refer to Psychic Vampirism, Auspex imitate real psychic power, like if mage use telepathy, that isn't real psychic power, it's magic imitating it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T04:35:04-08:00","id":1530630,"title":"","content":"Supernatural merits and merit templates are rare, and lost if one becomes a kindred, so I suspect mostly the answer is they don't think of them because they don't know about them. Those few vampires who do know about the probably find them to be a curiosity and potentially useful if they could get their hands on one. I imagine the Ordo Dracul might be the most interested in them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T05:06:08-08:00","id":1530633,"title":"","content":"A starting Psychic Vampire is actually a lot more powerful that your starting Vampire, if you give them like the same amount point to spend on character creation, so Psychic Vampire with 19 merit point, but even with only 7, the Psychic Vampire can hide themself with humanity perfectly without the use of Blush of Life, while getting to live forever without having to go into torpor, and don't suffer from burning in the sun, fire doesn't cause aggravated damage, have a lot more potential for other power, if they choose Vampiric Potency, attribute can go above 5 without having to wait 50 years, and doesn't suffer any of it downside, they doesn't suffer from the Beast, have power that can imitate some of the discipline while being a lot cheaper, like the only thing that stopping them is that they can't steal vitae from Vampire, and if they have Breath Stealer, they know that the Vampire isn't human, if the Vampire doesn't use Blush of Life, which would still make the Psychic Vampire suspicous that they can only steal the Willpower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28270,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","user":"Yumlum","date":". 02-12-2024, 08:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T06:28:01-08:00","id":1530636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1530606-how-are-the-clan-and-the-covenant-opinion-on-psychic-vampire?p=1530633#post1530633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A starting Psychic Vampire is actually a lot more powerful that your starting Vampire, if you give them like the same amount point to spend on character creation, so Psychic Vampire with 19 merit point, but even with only 7, the Psychic Vampire can hide themself with humanity perfectly without the use of Blush of Life, while getting to live forever without having to go into torpor, and don't suffer from burning in the sun, fire doesn't cause aggravated damage, have a lot more potential for other power, if they choose Vampiric Potency, attribute can go above 5 without having to wait 50 years, and doesn't suffer any of it downside, they doesn't suffer from the Beast, have power that can imitate some of the discipline while being a lot cheaper, like the only thing that stopping them is that they can't steal vitae from Vampire, and if they have Breath Stealer, they know that the Vampire isn't human, if the Vampire doesn't use Blush of Life, which would still make the Psychic Vampire suspicous that they can only steal the Willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>If your argument is that a psychic vampire house ruled to have a huge chunk of extra xp is stronger than a fledgling who was embraced last night, I don't think anyone would argue with you. But if you're saying they're stronger than vampires can become you're wildly incorrect. Vampires have an incredibly high ceiling for power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T07:01:42-08:00","id":1530639,"title":"","content":"How high is the Vampire ceiling for power? But I think Psychic Vampire have an advantage in the fact that they can live forever with no downside, the only downside is that they need a lot more Ephemera, but any Psychic Vampire who live that long, can probably steal willpower instead of life force from the victim, who I don't see any reference of needing to be human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T07:21:37-08:00","id":1530641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1530606-how-are-the-clan-and-the-covenant-opinion-on-psychic-vampire?p=1530639#post1530639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How high is the Vampire ceiling for power? But I think Psychic Vampire have an advantage in the fact that they can live forever with no downside, the only downside is that they need a lot more Ephemera, but any Psychic Vampire who live that long, can probably steal willpower instead of life force from the victim, who I don't see any reference of needing to be human.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires ceiling is pretty much as high as the GM wants it to be. New Disciplines, blood magics, and coils are being created and devotions can be created as well. <br /> <br /> The psychic vampire's needs for ephemera scale. A young psychic vampire can spend very little ephemera the first year they wish to stop aging, but an older one might have to spend a thousand or more ephemera, meanwhile the vampire's need for blood remains constant. <br /> <br /> Also, psychic vampires remain human, lethal damage will always be a threat, their stores of energy will always be limited, their stats will always be limited, etc. For comparison, a vampire at blood potency 10 can store 75 viate, a psychic vampire can store something like 10 maximum? Psychic vampires don't have a supernatural potency either (IIRC) so will always be weaker at resisting effects / clash of wills than vampires. And a powerful vampire can reduce the psychic vampire's dice pool down to nothing more than a chance di if the psychic vampire wishes to feed on the vampire's willpower. <br /> <br /> Now don't take me as saying that psychic vampires are weak. I don't think they are. I've argued that they're as strong if not stronger than some of the immortal types listed in mummy just that they're not as powerful as a full splat, and that's okay. I don't think they're meant to be as powerful as a full splat, they're just a fun twist a mortal character can have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T07:49:48-08:00","id":1530643,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1530606-how-are-the-clan-and-the-covenant-opinion-on-psychic-vampire?p=1530641#post1530641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Word*</div> </div> </div> </div>That can be said for Supernatural Merit as well.<br /> <br /> They only need to spend Ephemera equal to their true current age, and if they don't for a year, they just age year older from when they first get the Psychic Vampirism, so realistically, an 3,000 years old Psychic Vampire while weaker than a 3,000 years old Vampire, only need to spend about 8 Ephemera per day to not age, while a 3,000 years old Vampire wouldn't really exist, since they would be either hunted down by other kindred who doesn't want to be eaten, or go into Torpor to reduce Blood Potency to 5.<br /> <br /> They can buy Supernatural Resistance, which is a Merit that is a substitute for Supernatural Tolerance, and they have a call Vampiric Potency that allow for Psychic to have attribute above 5, if you spend Ephemera, and can be purchase multiple time, for multiple attribute, which make the Max Ephemera that a Psychic Vampire can store be 15, but only for a scene, the Constant max is 10.<br /> <br /> I think that any Vampire who know about Psychic Vampire would probably want them, but they also would be cautious around them, because when you try to blood bond, or feed on them, they can try to drain you of willpower, and maybe even try to have something similiar to blood bond back to you, and they can potentially be more powerful than you realized.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T19:42:45-08:00","id":1530700,"title":"","content":"The Clan Stereotypes of Psychic Vampire.<br /> Daeva: I envy them, they can still enjoy all of the pleasure of being Mortal, I will make sure to savor your blood.<br /> Gangrel: Imitator of a Greator Beast.<br /> Mekhet: They may hide themselve within the herd, but their shadow is dark, and it's reveal what is hidden.<br /> Nosferatu: Behide their mask of Motality, hide a soul more rotten than any of us.<br /> Venture: Potentially useful, but can be dangerous if not handle correctly.<br /> <br /> The Covenant Sterotypes of Psychic Vampire.<br /> The Carthian Movement: They aren't exactly us, but their strong connection to humanity, might be what we need.<br /> The Circle of the Crone: Join us, and become the real deal.<br /> The Invictus: Perfect at hiding within plain sight, and potential danger to us.<br /> The Lancea et Sanctum: They use their gift, not for the Will of God, but for their own selfish human want, condem them.<br /> The Ordo Dracul: Fasinating, I wonder if they can steal Vitae?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-14T21:26:42-08:00","id":1530867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1530606-how-are-the-clan-and-the-covenant-opinion-on-psychic-vampire?p=1530611#post1530611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I like to know, what does each of the Clan, The Covenant, and Vampire in general think of Psychic Vampire, the closest I've seen of a Psychic Vampire in Requiem is Amara, but that is only a single person rather than Psychic Vampire itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, having opinions would require some degree of familiarity or at least awareness, i'd say. What is there on psychic vampires in Requiem, for starters? Who or what is this Amara you speak of?<br /> <br /> No, more importantly, what would be the definition of a &quot;Psychic Vampire&quot; in the first place? Because the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Psychic_vampire\" target=\"_blank\">wiki one</a> while a start can also be quite slippery and vague.<br /> Does any act of feeding on a person's lifeforce without actually biting them count? Because <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Breath-Drinking\" target=\"_blank\">some</a> kindred at least can do that.<br /> Would consuming someone's <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Hamartiaphage\" target=\"_blank\">sins</a> or <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Mnemovores\" target=\"_blank\">memories</a> count? Because vampires familiar with those, or at least critters that can do some of these things, we have examples of.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1530606-how-are-the-clan-and-the-covenant-opinion-on-psychic-vampire?p=1530619#post1530619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> When I mean &quot;Psychic Vampire&quot;, I refer to Psychic Vampirism, Auspex imitate real psychic power, like if mage use telepathy, that isn't real psychic power, it's magic imitating it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dr. Vincent Moon, succeful writer &amp; guru on occult/psychic phenomena and major character from Mekhet: Shadows in the Dark would probably want to have very pointed and strong words to exchange with you on this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, &quot;imitate real psychic power&quot; is kind of a @$$backwards way to go at qualifying/separating things, since &quot;psychic phenomena&quot; as a label has existed since the XVIII-XIX century while Mekhet are apparently millenia old at least. Not to mention the concept of psychic/paranormal phenomena on itself is something that gained form <i>as an attempt to fit the supernatural</i> into a sort of scientific framework, so handwaving away the magical/supernatural is.... kind of sketchy.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, back to the starting point, what is your definition of psychic vampire in the first place - what are you working from as a base concept of sorts...<br /> <br /> Would it be &quot;must not be undead&quot;? Because if it so, non-kindred variants of breath drinkers, mnemovores or sin-eaters (the mythologies version, not Geisters), maybe with some crosspolination with the Cihuateteo &amp; Ghouls (from Wicked Dead) or the Sons of Phobos (from Blood Sorcery) might be acceptable?<br /> Also, what are your thoughts on the possibility of a <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Mastigos\" target=\"_blank\">Mastigos</a> legacy? That definitely could fit the &quot;psychic&quot; and &quot;vampiric/draining&quot; labels to a tee.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-14T22:12:03-08:00","id":1530869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1530606-how-are-the-clan-and-the-covenant-opinion-on-psychic-vampire?p=1530633#post1530633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like to know, what does each of the Clan, The Covenant, and Vampire in general think of Psychic Vampire, the closest I've seen of a Psychic Vampire in Requiem is Amara, but that is only a single person rather than Psychic Vampire itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, having opinions would require some degree of familiarity or at least awareness, i'd say. What is there on psychic vampires in Requiem, for starters? Who or what is this Amara you speak of?<br /> <br /> No, more importantly, what would be the definition of a &quot;Psychic Vampire&quot; in the first place? Because the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Psychic_vampire\" target=\"_blank\">wiki one</a> while a start can also be quite slippery and vague.<br /> Does any act of feeding on a person's lifeforce without actually biting them count? Because <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Breath-Drinking\" target=\"_blank\">some</a> kindred at least can do that.<br /> Would consuming someone's <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Hamartiaphage\" target=\"_blank\">sins</a> or <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Mnemovores\" target=\"_blank\">memories</a> count? Because vampires familiar with those, or at least critters that can do some of these things, we have examples of.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1530606-how-are-the-clan-and-the-covenant-opinion-on-psychic-vampire?p=1530633#post1530633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When I mean &quot;Psychic Vampire&quot;, I refer to Psychic Vampirism, Auspex imitate real psychic power, like if mage use telepathy, that isn't real psychic power, it's magic imitating it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dr. Vincent Moon, succeful writer &amp; guru on occult/psychic phenomena and major character from Mekhet: Shadows in the Dark would probably want to have very pointed and strong words to exchange with you on this. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, &quot;imitate real psychic power&quot; is kind of a @$$backwards way to go at qualifying/separating things, since &quot;psychic phenomena&quot; as a label has existed since the XVIII-XIX century while Mekhet are apparently millenia old at least. Not to mention the concept of psychic/paranormal phenomena on itself is something that gained form <i>as an attempt to fit the supernatural</i> into a sort of scientific framework, so handwaving away the magical/supernatural is.... kind of sketchy.<br /> <br /> <br /> So, back to the starting point, what is your definition of psychic vampire in the first place - what are you working from as a base concept of sorts...<br /> <br /> Would it be &quot;must not be undead&quot;? Because if it so, non-kindred variants of breath drinkers, mnemovores or sin-eaters (the mythologies version, not Geisters), maybe with some crosspolination with the Cihuateteo &amp; Ghouls (from Wicked Dead) or the Sons of Phobos (from Blood Sorcery) might be acceptable?<br /> Also, what are your thoughts on the possibility of a <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Mastigos\" target=\"_blank\">Mastigos</a> legacy? That definitely could fit the &quot;psychic&quot; and &quot;vampiric/draining&quot; labels to a tee.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1530606-how-are-the-clan-and-the-covenant-opinion-on-psychic-vampire?p=1530633#post1530633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A starting Psychic Vampire is actually a lot more powerful that your starting Vampire, if you give them like the same amount point to spend on character creation, so Psychic Vampire with 19 merit point, but even with only 7, the Psychic Vampire can hide themself with humanity perfectly without the use of Blush of Life, while getting to live forever without having to go into torpor, and don't suffer from burning in the sun, fire doesn't cause aggravated damage, have a lot more potential for other power, if they choose Vampiric Potency, attribute can go above 5 without having to wait 50 years, and doesn't suffer any of it downside, they doesn't suffer from the Beast, have power that can imitate some of the discipline while being a lot cheaper, like the only thing that stopping them is that they can't steal vitae from Vampire, and if they have Breath Stealer, they know that the Vampire isn't human, if the Vampire doesn't use Blush of Life, which would still make the Psychic Vampire suspicous that they can only steal the Willpower.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pardon the ignorance, but what book are you referencing? I remember Second Sight, but some of the psychic merits you mentioned seem to come from some other source.<br /> Also, as an aside, white room can reach upon the sky and beyond with infinite White Room resources.<br /> <br /> That on itself does not make a template any less limited by default or more importantly for this discussion, minor and obscure from a canon/lore perspective. The why and how of something making the jump of &quot;people with some merits&quot; into actual minor template (like some of the Wicked Dead or antagonists in Geist or Mummy) or even perhaps greater template, that calls for a lot of buildupm lore/setting-wise specially.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-15-2024, 01:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-14T23:05:01-08:00","id":1530872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1530606-how-are-the-clan-and-the-covenant-opinion-on-psychic-vampire?p=1530869#post1530869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Word*</div> </div> </div> </div>The only closest to Psychic Vampire I can find in Requiem is Amara, and she is from Night Horror Spill Blood, she use to be test subject of Ordo Dracul, before escaping it.<br /> <br /> I mean the Psychic Vampire Supernatural Merit Template from Hurt Locker, sure there is a lot of 'Psychic Vampire' like Undead in Vampire the Requiem, but non of those are actually name 'Psychic Vampire'<br /> <br /> Auspex isn't true Psychic Power because it's limited in it's power and capabilities, why do you think Ordo Dracul have a Coil dedicated to bringing back people Psychic Vampire before the Embrace?<br /> <br /> And the Book I'm refering to is Hurt Locker.<br /> <br /> I'm specifically have been refering to Psychic Vampire this whole time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28270,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","user":"Yumlum","date":". 02-15-2024, 02:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}